[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710055610","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3710055610","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3710055610,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dIvS6","user":{"login":"Dragnaros92","id":154672228,"node_id":"U_kgDOCTgcZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154672228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92","html_url":"https://github.com/Dragnaros92","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T11:31:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T11:31:20Z","body":"this fix works and results in a returned collision but it is inconsistent with godot physics.\r\ngodot physics ignores the orthogonal normals\r\nthis fix returns the orthogonal normals as hit.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3710055610/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3712967112","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3712967112","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3712967112,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dT2HI","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T03:28:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T22:52:32Z","body":"@Dragnaros92 Well this does fix the linked issue, which is that the method will return no collision in the mrp.\r\n\r\nThis new separate issue you are describing seems to be related to the project setting `physics/jolt_physics_3d/collisions/collision_margin_fraction` or the `margin` property of the collision shapes. Setting either of these to `0` makes the collision with the `Platform` cube go away. Collision margins are discussed in the docs here: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.html#collision-margins","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3712967112/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714024520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3714024520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3714024520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dX4RI","user":{"login":"Dragnaros92","id":154672228,"node_id":"U_kgDOCTgcZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154672228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92","html_url":"https://github.com/Dragnaros92","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dragnaros92/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-06T10:00:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T10:00:04Z","body":"this is clearly over my head but i think filtering out the orthogonal face there is the right call but i do not understand why it does not detect the next collision.\r\n\r\nthe maintainer should know best and decide in the review.\r\n\r\neither way i really appreciate your effort @Kaleb-Reid . thank you.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3714024520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3764011732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3764011732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3764011732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gWkLU","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T15:25:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T15:25:00Z","body":"This is indeed not the correct fix. You can see why if you add this to the Character script:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif result.get_collision_count() > 0:\r\n\t\tprint(\"Collider: \", result.get_collider().name)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this fix, you can see that godot physics will print 'Floor' as colliding object while jolt physics will print 'Platform'. So godot has ignored the platform because of the normal and jolt hasn't.\r\n\r\nI will post my analysis in #114605 shortly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3764011732/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765030178","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3765030178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3765030178,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gac0i","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T07:56:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T07:57:10Z","body":"@jrouwe I dont think you can compare GodotPhysics3D and Jolt in regards to this issue because this issue doesn't happen on master with Jolt (from what I could find) if you disable the collision margin and GodotPhysics doesn't support collision margin. I looked at your analysis in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114605 and the issue seems to run deeper than your fix goes because if you change the body to a RigidBody3D instead of a CharacterBody3D it gets stuck on the `Platform` cube edge when it falls while in GodotPhysics3D it doesn't. Disabling the collision margin also changes the behaviour when using Jolt in this scenario.\r\n\r\nI also vaguely remember another issue which is probably related which I think @mihe responded to where a body would get stuck on edges of \"chunks\" when using Jolt and the cause was related to having a collision margin on the chunks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765030178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765101234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3765101234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3765101234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gauKy","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T09:32:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T09:32:05Z","body":"I didn't test how collision margins affect this, but it's quite likely that that changes things as normal calculations are very sensitive to small changes in initial conditions. I think the main problem (which my 'fix' doesn't address) is:\r\n\r\nIf you have some sort of collision filtering in `_body_motion_collide` that is not present in `_body_motion_cast` then there will always be a case where `_body_motion_cast` finds a collision that `_body_motion_collide` ignores. Since that stops the sweep, we will miss collisions further along the sweep. So I think changing the filter in `_body_motion_collide` is not the solution as it just shifts the problem to another edge case (unless the filter is changed in such a way that it never filters anything, but there was probably a good reason for adding a filter in the first place).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765101234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765128096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114611#issuecomment-3765128096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114611","id":3765128096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ga0ug","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T10:05:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T10:05:31Z","body":"@jrouwe I agree somewhat. I think that the filters where they are now in `_body_motion_collide` is incorrect because this causes the bug in #114605. Either the filters happen for both cases (doesn't fix the RigidBody3D scenario), or they should be removed and instead happen further up in the collision detection to fix other cases as well. From what I remember GodotPhysics3D didn't have any filters in its equivalent `_body_motion_collide`. I'm not sure why it implemented as is Jolt. Having more background as to why they were put there would probably be helpful.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765128096/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]